  "content": {
    "id": "p25-q5-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "5",
    "prompt": "",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p25-q5-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find the minimum value of $x^2+(x+1)^2$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac12$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2+(x+1)^2&=2x^2+2x+1\\\\x^2+(x+1)^2&=2\\left(x^2+x+\\frac14\\right)+\\frac12\\\\x^2+(x+1)^2&=2\\left(x+\\frac12\\right)^2+\\frac12\\end{align*}$$\nSince the squared term is non-negative, the minimum is $\\dfrac12$, attained when $x=-\\dfrac12$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 35
      },
      {
        "id": "p25-q5-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find the minimum value of $x^2+(x+1)^2+(x+2)^2$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2+(x+1)^2+(x+2)^2&=3x^2+6x+5\\\\x^2+(x+1)^2+(x+2)^2&=3(x^2+2x+1)+2\\\\x^2+(x+1)^2+(x+2)^2&=3(x+1)^2+2\\end{align*}$$\nSince the squared term is non-negative, the minimum is $2$, attained when $x=-1$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p25-q5-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Consider the quadratic function $y=x^2+(x+a)^2$. Given that the minimum value of $y$ is $18$, find the value of $a$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$a=\\pm6$\n\nCompleting the square gives a minimum of $\\dfrac{a^2}{2}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y&=2x^2+2ax+a^2\\\\y&=2\\left(x^2+ax+\\frac{a^2}{4}\\right)+\\frac{a^2}{2}\\\\y&=2\\left(x+\\frac a2\\right)^2+\\frac{a^2}{2}\\end{align*}$$\nThe minimum is $\\dfrac{a^2}{2}$, attained when $x=-\\dfrac a2$. Hence,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{a^2}{2}&=18\\\\a^2&=36\\\\a&=\\pm6\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 50
      }
    ]
  },
